# Ignore everything by default
/**/*

# Allow all directories for traversal
!**/

# Deny common build/cache directories
**/.DS_Store
**/target/
**/.cache/
**/.git/
# Buck2 persistent on-disk sqlite dir-cache (buckconfig.d/cache.buckconfig dir = .buck-cache/sqlite).
# Lives outside buck-out intentionally to survive `buck2 clean`; must be gitignored.
**/.buck-cache/

# Deny Nix symlinks and generated files
**/result
**/result-*

# Deny temporary/log files
**/*.log

# Root level files
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/justfile
!/default.nix
!/here
!/.envrc
!/.editorconfig

# Rust
!/**/*.rs
!/**/rustfmt.toml
# Workspace + crate manifests required for cargo / rustService builds.
# (Flake source filtering follows git — without these, `nix build .#server`
# has Cargo.lock but no Cargo.toml and cargo fails immediately.)
!/Cargo.toml
!/Cargo.lock
!/workspace/**/Cargo.toml
# Crates under /crates need the same allowance — without it a new crate's
# manifest is silently ignored and the workspace fails to load.
!/crates/**/Cargo.toml
# Manifests that tests scaffold at runtime stay ignored.
/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/Cargo.toml

# C/C++ parser fixtures
!/compiler/src/core/clang/tests/**/*.c
!/compiler/src/core/clang/tests/**/*.cpp
!/compiler/src/core/clang/tests/**/compile_commands.json

# Vendored C sources that are the ONLY definition of symbols the Rust tree
# declares as `extern "C"`. These were absent from the checkout, and because
# both qdrant-edge build scripts warned-and-skipped instead of failing, the
# gap surfaced ~200 lines later as six undefined symbols at `driver`'s link
# step (LIMITATIONS L7). `build_common.rs::require_vendored_source` now makes
# that a hard build error, but the error only helps if the sources can be
# committed in the first place — the blanket `/**/*` rule above silently
# swallowed them, so `git add` no-opped and every clean checkout rebuilt the
# same breakage. ~37 KB total.
!/workspace/vendor/**/cpp/**/*.c
!/workspace/vendor/**/cpp/**/*.h

# The Vaporetto tokenizer model `japanese.rs` pulls in via `include_bytes!`.
# What was on disk was a 4-byte file containing the ASCII text `STUB`, which
# compiles cleanly and then panics inside `Model::read_slice(MODEL).unwrap()`
# on the first Japanese tokenization. The real artifact is 817,859 bytes and
# is verified against `MODEL_CHECKSUM`, declared in `japanese.rs` itself, so
# a wrong or truncated copy fails loudly rather than at first use. Binary and
# large for a source tree, tracked deliberately: the alternative is an
# unpinned network fetch in a build script, or the stub coming back.
!/workspace/vendor/**/tokenizer/*.model

# DoltLite vendoring: the pin and the fetcher, NOT the amalgamation.
#
# `manifest.toml` pins upstream v0.11.41 (commit e2be0af1…) plus the archive
# and per-file sha256s; `fetch.nu` fetches, verifies **before** extracting, and
# installs — the same verify-or-abort discipline as `corpus/fetch.nu`, so no
# build script ever performs an unpinned network fetch. Without these two in
# the tree the pin is unreproducible and `build.rs` finds no amalgamation, at
# which point `sys.rs` emits no C externs and every `Connection::open` returns
# `EngineError::EngineNotLinked` — i.e. the whole guard degrades to "no engine"
# rather than to the silent wrong-engine bug it exists to prevent.
#
# Deliberately NOT allow-listed, and this is a policy choice rather than an
# oversight: `doltlite.c` (11.7 MB), `doltlite.h` (695 KB), `doltliteext.h`
# (39 KB). All three are *generated*, hash-pinned by the manifest above, and
# restored by `nu workspace/vendor/doltlite/fetch.nu` in one command. Contrast
# the Vaporetto tokenizer model below, which IS committed: that artifact has no
# upstream fetcher and its absence produced a 4-byte `STUB` that compiled fine
# and panicked at first use. Here the absence is typed and loud, so the 11.7 MB
# buys nothing.
!/workspace/vendor/doltlite/manifest.toml
!/workspace/vendor/doltlite/fetch.nu

# Nix
!/flake.nix
!/flake.lock
# Shared helpers under build/nix (not a sub-flake — root flake imports them).
!/build/nix/**/*.nix
!/build/nix/buck2-artifact.json
!/build/nix/BUCK
# Workspace package recipes + images.
!/workspace/**/*.nix
# Integration checks (Nix glue + Nushell scripts/modules).
!/tests/**/*.nix
!/tests/**/*.nu
# Reproducible corpus manifest and fallback script (declarative package sources).
!/corpus/
!/corpus/**/*.toml
!/corpus/**/*.nu

# Data and Configuration Artifacts
# TODO: Remove from pipeline (currently used for debugging/regression tracking)
!/**/example.json
!/**/out.json
!/**/docs.json
!/**/schema.json

# Documentation
!/**/*.md

# Trustfall schema and query sources
!/**/*.graphql
!/**/*.trustfall

# Go / Java oracle producer sources. Unlike the Rust producer (compiled from
# committed .rs), the Go and Java oracles ship as source compiled by Buck2's
# go_binary / java_library. They must be tracked or fresh checkouts / git
# worktrees build an empty target ("not package main" / "expected exactly one
# default output").
# NOTE: `workspace/compiler/compile/` no longer exists (folded into
# `workspace/compiler/languages/` — see git history at 23530d7). These two
# patterns are dead but harmless; kept so a future revert of that migration
# does not silently lose tracking. The Go oracle's new home is covered below.
!/workspace/compiler/compile/**/*.go
!/workspace/compiler/compile/**/*.java
!/workspace/compiler/compile/**/go.mod
!/workspace/compiler/compile/**/go.sum
# Go oracle source at its post-migration home. The compiled `nudox-go-oracle`
# binary this produces is NOT allow-listed here — it stays denied by the
# default-deny rule at the top of this file, same as every other build
# artifact.
!/workspace/compiler/languages/go/oracle/*.go
!/workspace/compiler/languages/go/oracle/go.mod
!/workspace/compiler/languages/go/oracle/go.sum
# Java oracle source at its post-migration home (JAVELIN restoration from git
# history at 23530d7^) — same reasoning as the Go oracle above: `javac`
# (via build.rs) compiles these two committed .java files at crate build
# time; the resulting `.class` files land under Cargo's own `OUT_DIR` and
# stay denied by the default-deny rule, same as every other build artifact.
!/workspace/compiler/languages/java/oracle/*.java

# C# Roslyn oracle — unlike Go and Java above, this was NOT recovered from
# history (only a BUCK file ever existed); it is new source and is the sole copy.
# Single-level `*` is deliberate: `**/` would also un-ignore `obj/**/*.g.cs` and
# the generated `AssemblyInfo.cs`, which must stay denied as build artifacts.
!/workspace/compiler/languages/csharp/oracle/*.cs
!/workspace/compiler/languages/csharp/oracle/oracle.csproj
!/workspace/compiler/languages/csharp/oracle/packages.lock.json
!/workspace/compiler/languages/csharp/tests/fixture/*.cs
!/workspace/compiler/languages/csharp/tests/fixture/fixture.csproj

# Producer test fixtures: source files for the TypeScript / Nix producers are
# committed (mirroring the committed Rust `.rs` fixtures). Manifests that tests
# scaffold at runtime (rust `Cargo.toml`) stay ignored; these are the inputs the
# producers read directly, so they must live in the tree.
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.ts
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.tsx
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.mts
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.cts
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.d.ts
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/package.json
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.nix
# Go / Java producer test fixtures (mirror the .ts / .nix fixtures above).
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.go
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/*.java
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/go.mod
!/workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/**/go.sum
# nudox-producer-java's own real-library fixture (Gson 2.11.0, vendored —
# see workspace/compiler/languages/java/tests/producer_tests.rs's module doc
# for exactly what is/isn't real Gson source) plus small hand-written-but-
# really-compiled supplementary fixtures (records/sealed/module-info; a JEP
# 467 probe). Committed, not `workspace/compiler/tests/fixtures/` above,
# because these are specific to this one producer crate. Committed at all —
# rather than fetched over the network at test time — so a fresh checkout can
# run `cargo test -p nudox-producer-java` hermetically.
!/workspace/compiler/languages/java/tests/fixtures/**/*.java
!/workspace/compiler/languages/java/tests/fixtures/**/LICENSE-gson.txt
# Index ingest test fixtures (moved from workspace/ingestor).
!/workspace/index/tests/fixtures/*.json

# The curated `cpp` alias seed. This is NOT a fixture — `ecosystem/cpp/alias.rs`
# pulls it in with `include_str!`, so it is a build input: without it the whole
# `index` crate fails to compile. The blanket `/**/*` rule at the top would
# swallow it, `git add` would silently no-op, and a fresh clone would be back to
# the "couldn't read cpp_alias_seed.ron" error that kept this crate from
# building at all.
!/workspace/index/ecosystem/assets/*.ron

# insta snapshot expectations (accepted `.snap` files) for the producer /
# renderer snapshot tests. These are the committed test baselines; insta's
# transient `.snap.new` pending files end in `.new` so this glob leaves them
# ignored.
!/**/*.snap

# Patch files for Buck2 genrules
!/**/*.patch

# Allow empty .keep files
!/**/.keep
!/.config/scripts/*.nu
# cargo-nextest configuration. Without this the blanket `/**/*` rule at the top
# swallows it, `git add .config/nextest.toml` silently no-ops, and a fresh clone
# gets no test groups at all — which is how the GUI and real-crate serialisation
# would quietly stop being enforced.
!/.config/nextest.toml
!/.config/nextest-gui.toml
!/.vscode/settings.json

## Cue
!/.config/**/*.cue

/.direnv
!/schema.yaml

# Devenv
!/devenv.yaml
!/devenv.nix
!/devenv.lock

# TODO: Remove when upstreamed
!/linkml

!/deno_doc/**/*

# Buck2 build system
!/.buckconfig
# cache.buckconfig is hard-included by .buckconfig (`<file:...>`); it must be in
# the tree or Buck2 fails to init ("Included file doesn't exist"). Track it so
# fresh checkouts / git worktrees get it.
!/buckconfig.d/
!/buckconfig.d/**
!/.buckroot
!/.buckversion
!/build/
!/build/**
!**/BUCK
!**/TARGETS
/buck-out/
/.buckcredentials
/rust-project.json
/prelude

.claude/worktrees/
/build/prelude
/build/third-party/tools
/build/third-party/vendor

# Writable Buck2 prelude (generated by build/setup-prelude.sh)
/build/prelude-local/
# Symlink to the pinned buck2.nix nix store path (created by devshell hook)
/build/nix-cell

# snowydeer deploy boundary (Phase 4) — vendored Buck2 + Python files
!/snowydeer/
!/snowydeer/**
# link_style constraints for snowydeer transition_to_static
!/constraints/
!/constraints/**
/.agent-wt
/build/third-party/.cargo
/build/third-party/.cargo-tmp

# Allow nested gitignores
!/**/.gitignore

# cargo-fuzz manifests and targets; generated corpora/artifacts stay ignored by
# fuzz/.gitignore.
!/fuzz/Cargo.toml
!/fuzz/fuzz_targets/**/*.rs
.real-crates/
# Captured frames from `cargo test --test screenshots` (workspace/gui). They are
# evidence, not source: regenerable in one command, and byte-unstable across
# machines because glyph rasterisation depends on the host font stack — so
# committing them would churn on every run while proving nothing a re-run
# cannot. The regeneration command lives in GUI-PROOF.md.
.shots/
